WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.350
Step out on the coldest morning, and your teeth chatter.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.490
Now write that feeling down as music.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:14.610
Three hundred years ago, Vivaldi did just that, in a violin concerto called Winter, from The Four Seasons.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:18.370
From its first bars, the orchestra seems to shiver.

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:20.970
But a violin has no teeth to chatter.

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:23.610
It is wood, strings and a bow.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:26.130
So how do you make a violin shiver?

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:32.390
In this mission, you'll meet the players: one solo violin against a small string orchestra.

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:42.150
You'll listen to the frozen opening, then to wind, stamping feet and chattering teeth, and find out what Vivaldi wrote down to make the cold bite.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:45.870
Your mission: explain how you make a violin shiver.
